<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    This is a separate, minimal, elevated-only executable (IR3/IKTD1) —
    never linked into Serpy.App.exe. It hosts the authenticated named-pipe
    server, verifies the runtime descriptor, and performs the actual
    `runas`-elevated copy/re-verify/launch of the vendor QEMU installer.
    It is Windows-only end to end: named pipes with ACL/impersonation,
    Authenticode verification, and NSIS installer launch are all Win32-only
    concerns, so AssemblyInfo.cs marks the whole assembly
    [SupportedOSPlatform("windows")] rather than per-file.

    The pipe server's DACL is built via a direct CreateNamedPipeW P/Invoke
    (see Program.cs) rather than the System.IO.Pipes.AccessControl package:
    that package's reference assembly did not resolve cleanly against this
    SDK's plain net10.0 targeting pack in this environment, and this repo's
    existing convention for Win32-security-sensitive code (HelperSignatureVerifier's
    WinVerifyTrust) is direct P/Invoke over an indirect wrapper anyway.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Serpy.Core\Serpy.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
